  </section>

  <section class="eva-how section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="eva-how-title">
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="section-head center reveal"><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h2 id="eva-how-title">From routine use to a longitudinal view.</h2></div>
      <div class="pipeline pipeline--eva reveal">
        <div class="pipeline__track" aria-hidden="true"><span class="pipeline__pulse"></span></div>
        <ol class="pipeline__steps eva-how-grid">
          <li class="pipeline__step" style="--n:0">
            <div class="pipeline__node eva-how-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48"><path d="M18 5h12a6 6 0 0 1 6 6v7l4 3v6l-4 3v7a6 6 0 0 1-6 6H18a6 6 0 0 1-6-6v-7l-4-3v-6l4-3v-7a6 6 0 0 1 6-6z"/><rect x="20.5" y="13" width="7" height="22" rx="3.5"/></svg></div>
            <span class="workflow-number">01</span>
            <h3>Use</h3><p>The pad is worn as part of the user’s normal menstrual routine.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pipeline__step" style="--n:1">
            <div class="pipeline__node eva-how-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48"><path d="M24 5c5.5 6.5 9 11.3 9 15.5a9 9 0 0 1-18 0C15 16.3 18.5 11.5 24 5z"/><path d="M10 41h28M14 41v-5M20 41v-5M28 41v-5M34 41v-5"/></svg></div>
            <span class="workflow-number">02</span>
            <h3>Sense</h3><p>Integrated electrochemical sensors interact with menstrual fluid and generate electrical signals.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pipeline__step" style="--n:2">
            <div class="pipeline__node eva-how-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48"><rect x="7" y="14" width="20" height="20" rx="6"/><circle cx="17" cy="25" r="1.7"/><path d="M32 19a7 7 0 0 1 0 10M36.5 15a13 13 0 0 1 0 18"/></svg></div>
            <span class="workflow-number">03</span>
            <h3>Interpret</h3><p>The reusable reader and data-processing system organize and analyze the sensor response.</p>
          </li>
          <li class="pipeline__step" style="--n:3">
            <div class="pipeline__node eva-how-icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48"><rect x="14" y="5" width="20" height="38" rx="5"/><path d="M18.5 31l4-5 3.5 3 4-7"/><circle cx="30" cy="22" r="1.7"/></svg></div>
            <span class="workflow-number">04</span>
            <h3>Understand</h3><p>The application presents longitudinal trends intended to support future health understanding and clinical research.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-technology-page section" id="eva-technology" aria-labelledby="eva-technology-title">
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="section-head split reveal">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Technology</p><h2 id="eva-technology-title">Advanced sensing, integrated into a familiar form.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-lead">EVA extends WE-Sensing’s broader sensing platform into a women’s health application while keeping the physical product and user experience central to the system design.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="eva-tech-layout">
        <figure class="eva-tech-architecture reveal"><img class="eva-tech-architecture__image" src="/assets/eva/web/eva-concept.webp" width="2200" height="1051" alt="EVA technology architecture from sensing interface to longitudinal interpretation" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure>
        <div class="eva-tech-modules" data-stagger>
          <article><span>01</span><div><h3>Electrochemical Sensing Interface</h3><p>Flexible sensor elements designed to respond to selected chemical changes in menstrual fluid.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>02</span><div><h3>Integrated Fluid Interaction</h3><p>A sensing region positioned within the pad architecture to interact with collected menstrual fluid.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>03</span><div><h3>Reusable Electronics</h3><p>A detachable reader designed to acquire signals from the disposable sensing pad.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>04</span><div><h3>Signal Interpretation</h3><p>Data-processing methods intended to transform complex sensor responses into longitudinal measurements and interpretable trends.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <ul class="eva-capabilities reveal" aria-label="Related WE-Sensing expertise"><li>Electrochemical sensing</li><li>Sensor materials</li><li>Custom electronics</li><li>Signal processing</li><li>Machine learning</li><li>Scalable fabrication</li></ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-development section" id="development" aria-labelledby="eva-development-title">
    <div class="page-width">
      <div class="section-head split reveal">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Development</p><h2 id="eva-development-title">A staged path from sensing feasibility to future launch.</h2></div>
        <p class="section-lead">The sequence below describes the intended development path. Individual stage status will be published only after formal project review.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="eva-roadmap reveal" data-eva-roadmap></ol>
      <div class="eva-development-disclaimer reveal"><span>Important</span><p>EVA is currently under development and is not available for clinical diagnosis or treatment decisions.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="eva-partnerships section" id="partnerships" aria-labelledby="eva-partnership-title">
    <div class="page-width eva-partnerships__grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">Partnerships</p>
        <h2 id="eva-partnership-title">Building EVA with scientific and clinical partners.</h2>
        <p>WE-Sensing welcomes focused conversations with teams whose expertise can help shape rigorous research, product development, and responsible translation.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-eva" href="/?inquiry=eva#contact">Discuss an EVA Partnership</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="eva-partnership-list reveal" data-eva-partnerships></ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="eva-footer-disclaimer" aria-label="EVA development disclaimer"><div class="page-width"><span>EVA development status</span><p>EVA is currently under development and is not available for clinical diagnosis or treatment decisions.</p></div></aside>
</article>
